        "accordion_hHjUgk": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Frequently asked questions",
            "content": "<p><strong>Which driver do I need?</strong><br/>Add up your strip wattage, then pick the driver where that total is 80% of the rating or less. KAYVA 480 Pro draws 12W per metre: up to 5 m takes the 80W, up to 10 m takes the 160W. For other strips, multiply W/m by metres and apply the same 80% rule.</p><p><strong>Can I run more than 10 m from one driver?</strong><br/>No. Over 10 m, use a second driver. Running a driver above its rating overheats it and shortens its life.</p><p><strong>Can I dim my strip with this driver?</strong><br/>Not on its own. It is a non-dimmable constant-voltage driver. To dim, add a 24V PWM dimmer between the driver output and the strip. The driver stays as it is; the dimmer does the dimming.</p><p><strong>Is this a plug-in adapter?<br/></strong>No. It is wired into the mains with screw terminals (Earth, Live, Neutral). There is no plug. Mains connection must be done by a licensed electrical worker.</p><p><strong>Can I use it outdoors or in a bathroom?</strong><br/>No. It is IP20, for dry indoor locations only. Mount it where air can move around it, such as inside the cove or above the false ceiling.<br/><br/><strong>Can two strips run from one driver?<br/></strong>Yes. The output side has two V+ and two V− terminals. Two runs can share one driver as long as their combined wattage stays within the 80% rule.</p><p><strong>Does it work with 12V strip?</strong><br/>No. This is a 24V driver. Connecting 12V strip will damage the strip. Check the printed voltage on your strip before ordering.<br/><br/><strong>Is it SAFETY Mark registered?</strong><br/>Yes. 80W is registered under 260198-15 and 160W under 260199-15, both printed on the unit. Tested to IEC 61347-2-13 by TÜV Rheinland. You can check the numbers on the Consumer Product Safety Office register.<br/><br/><strong>What is the warranty?</strong> 3 years. Keep your order number.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
